{#
  T-4.21 — «تنسيقات جاهزة من أملاس», the centred image carousel.

  | Variable          | Type    | Description                                                      |
  |-------------------|---------|------------------------------------------------------------------|
  | items             | array   | List of slides                                                   |
  | items[].url       | string  |                                                                  |
  | items[].link_type | ?String | category,product,offers,page,external_link,brand                 |
  | items[].image.url | string  |                                                                  |
  | items[].image.alt | string  |                                                                  |
  | title             | ?string | Section title, when the platform supplies one                    |
  | position          | Int     | Sorting number start from zero                                   |

  UPSTREAM'S CARRIER IS KEPT. `salla-slider type="carousel" centered` is this
  shape exactly — a centred slide with its neighbours partly visible — which is
  why T-1.03 kept the `component-photos-slider` flag. Nothing here replaces it.
  What changes is everything around it: a real heading, real alt text, reserved
  dimensions, and autoplay that can be stopped.

  THE TITLE IS NEVER A LITERAL, and it has two possible sources because the
  platform owns this section's fields and the theme cannot add one. If the
  platform passes `title`, that wins. If it does not, the `photos_slider_title`
  theme setting supplies it. Either way a merchant changes the wording without a
  developer, which is the rule; and if neither is set the heading is simply
  omitted rather than filled with something invented.

  ALT TEXT COMES FROM THE MERCHANT'S OWN FIELD. Upstream wrote
  `alt="{{ store.name }} image-slider-{{ index }}"` — the same words on every
  slide, which is worse than nothing because a screen reader reads all of them.
  `items[].image.alt` is documented and is what a merchant filled in; empty
  renders `alt=""` and marks the slide decorative, which is honest.

  THE INDICATOR IS T-4.03'S OWN CONTROL, NOT SWIPER'S PAGINATION. Both artboards
  draw a full-width track with a third-width thumb sitting at the active slide —
  the middle third while the middle photo is centred (mobile SVG y3190, desktop
  y4024). Swiper's `progressbar` was half-width here and grows a fill from the
  start (1/3 → 2/3 → full); it never moves a thumb, so it could not draw that
  (home audit, 2026-10-15). `home.js` drives T-4.03's track and thumb from the
  swiper's progress instead, so there are no focusable bullets and no second
  indicator implementation.
#}
{% set photos_title = title|default(theme.settings.get('photos_slider_title')) %}

{% if items|length %}
<section data-testid="store-home-photos-slider"
         class="s-block photos-carousel container {{ is_repeated ? 'repeated-block' : '' }}"
         data-autoplay-scope>
        <div class="s-block__panel">
        {% if photos_title %}
            {% include 'components.ui.section-header' with {
                title: photos_title,
                align: 'start',
                level: 2
            } %}
        {% endif %}

        {# The stage positions the pause control over the photographs, the way the
           hero carries its own, instead of against the section's corner, where it
           floated outside the panel's edge (Salla review, 2026-10-20). #}
        <div class="photos-carousel__stage">
            <salla-slider
              type="carousel"
              class="photos-carousel__slider"
              centered
              auto-play
              slider-config='{"breakpoints":{"768":{"centeredSlides":false,"slidesPerView":2,"spaceBetween":16},"1024":{"centeredSlides":false,"slidesPerView":3,"spaceBetween":16}}}'
              id="photos-{{ position }}-slider">
              <div slot="items">
                {% for item in items %}
                  <div class="swiper-slide photos-carousel__slide">
                    <a href="{{ item.url }}">
                      <img src="{{ item.image.url }}"
                           alt="{{ item.image.alt|default('') }}"
                           width="1200"
                           height="900"
                           {% if loop.first %}loading="eager"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
                           decoding="async">
                    </a>
                  </div>
                {% endfor %}
              </div>
            </salla-slider>

            {# Autoplay is on for this section, so the control is unconditional here —
               unlike the hero, where it is a merchant choice. WCAG 2.2.2, Level A. #}
            {% if items|length > 1 %}
                <button type="button"
                        class="photos-carousel__autoplay-toggle"
                        data-autoplay-toggle
                        aria-pressed="false"
                        aria-label="{{ trans('theme.common.pause_autoplay') }}">
                    {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'pause' } %}
                </button>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# Decorative: the slides carry the position. Its box is reserved from
           the first paint (no `hidden`), so the swiper arriving moves nothing. #}
        {% if items|length > 1 %}
            <div class="product-carousel__indicator" data-carousel-indicator="swiper" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="product-carousel__thumb"></span>
            </div>
        {% endif %}

    </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
